WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:04.430
After years of waiting, "The Batman" has finally
swooped into theaters.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:08.580
It's been a long road for this new version
of the Dark Knight to make its way to the

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:13.150
big screen, as the production was hit with
pandemic-related delays and setbacks.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:18.520
Robert Pattinson himself reportedly caught
COVID-19 during filming, so it's a minor miracle

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.040
that Warner Bros. has finally been able to
release the Matt Reeves-directed movie.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.670
Thankfully, the film pushes its cast of DC
heroes and villains in new directions, many

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:30.210
of which should even surprise longtime fans.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:34.620
The action kicks off in Bruce Wayne's second
year of crime fighting, so audiences don't

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.350
have to sit through yet another origin story.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:41.440
When a sadistic individual called the Riddler
starts targeting the corrupt officials of

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.940
Gotham, Batman sets out to stop his violent
war before the villain can hurt the rest of

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.940
the city.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:51.000
The Caped Crusader also crosses paths with
some other iconic characters from the Batman

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.230
mythos, as he gets help from Lt. James Gordon
and Catwoman aka Selina Kyle.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:01:01.960
He even goes up against two other iconic Bat-villains
— Penguin and Carmine Falcone — who are

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.610
at the heart of organized crime in Gotham.

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:07.580
That said, there's never any doubt who the
big bad of this film is.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:11.770
When it comes to the film's cryptic serial
killer, director Matt Reeves and co-writer

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:15.610
Peter Craig take a new approach to the riddle-obsessed
villain.

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:18.610
Before we go any further, be warned: Spoilers
ahead!

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:22.800
Let's get the most obvious change out of the
way first: the Riddler's new duds.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.600
Gone are the days of bright green spandex
with question marks painted all over — no,

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.750
this version of the villain takes a more tactical
approach to his look.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:35.230
He sports a dark green military jacket with
a similarly colored hoodie underneath.

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:39.130
Then there's his incredibly creepy mask that
he wears with transparent glasses over the

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:43.230
top to mask his real identity — which we'll
get to later on.

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:48.530
After the first teaser for the film arrived
back in August 2020, comics writer Nick Derington

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:52.910
took to Twitter to point out that Riddler's
headgear is actually an Extreme Cold Weather

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:55.160
Mask used by the U.S. military.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:58.730
So why does Riddler take a DIY approach to
his terrifying look?

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:02.730
Well, for starters he doesn't have the same
funds as Bruce Wayne to create a high-tech

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:07.060
suit — so he probably shops in army surplus
stores for his gear.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:11.200
Let's not forget that this version of the
villain is much more of a homegrown terrorist

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.860
than Jim Carrey's gleeful mischief-maker in
"Batman Forever."

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:19.660
He's also a huge departure from the sharp-suited
version of the character in the "Gotham" TV

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:20.660
series.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:25.060
The small screen's Riddler is also a former
GCPD forensic scientist.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:29.370
Although he clearly enjoys taunting Gotham
in his livestreams — a flamboyant, eccentric

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:33.060
Riddler wouldn't fit into this universe that
Matt Reeves is building.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.420
The Riddler also tells the hero that his mask
allows him to become his true self.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:41.850
It's all an attempt to bond with Batman, as
he points out that the Caped Crusader's persona

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.500
is also his true face.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:47.209
It's the classic "we're the same, you and
I" approach to connecting the hero and the

00:02:47.209 --> 00:02:48.209
villain.

00:02:48.209 --> 00:02:51.680
There's another surprising difference in the
Riddler's character from what DC fans might

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:54.510
expect: His name isn't Edward Nigma.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:58.780
This time around the villain uses his birth
name, Edward Nashton, a choice that's mainly

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:02.810
about making sure these characters feel natural
to the world of "The Batman."

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:05.740
The “E.Nigma” joke wouldn't work as well
here.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.310
It just feels kinda silly.

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:11.490
Sure, Nashton's job as an accountant is the
reason behind his war on corruption in the

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.710
first place, but the Riddler persona is who
he really is.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:19.349
Plus, he's already projecting majorly enigmatic
vibes even without the pseudonym.

00:03:19.349 --> 00:03:23.300
When the police eventually manage to arrest
the Riddler, his wallet is filled with a couple

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:27.610
of ID cards — so they're not 100% sure who
he actually is.

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:32.090
Riddler's detached personality, his unhinged
crimes, and his bizarre costume even call

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:34.170
back to a real-life serial killer.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:36.310
When speaking to MovieMaker, Reeves said,

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:40.270
"The premise of the movie is that the Riddler
is kind of molded in an almost Zodiac Killer

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:41.340
sort of mode."

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:45.990
It's easy to see the connection, since the
Riddler sends messages written in code, much

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:50.170
like the Zodiac Killer who terrified San Francisco
in the 1970s.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:55.300
Thankfully, Alfred Pennyworth happens to be
a master code-breaker, which is hugely helpful

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:59.050
when he and Bruce are picking apart Riddler's
cryptic messages.

